# Ops Surface Design Boundaries

Three intentional design languages. Do not unify them.

## Studio — Mission Control

- Routes: `/ops/studio/*`, Browser+ 2 ops shell (`.ops-page--bp2`)
- Theme: dark blue, cinematic, `rs-studio-*` tokens
- CSS: `studio-design-tokens.css`, `studio-design-utilities.css`, `studio.css`
- Use: `rs-studio-panel`, `rs-studio-review-panel`, department pages

## Public Experience — Museum

- Routes: `/experience/*`
- Theme: immersive, edge-to-edge patron UI
- Not ops tooling; not Studio blue

## VirtualDJ Browser — Library utility

- Routes: `/ops/browser-plus` (`.browser-plus-page`, `.browser-plus`)
- Theme: lightweight, data-first, VDJ red/black utility tables
- CSS: `browser-plus.css`, `browser-product-tokens.css` only
- **Never** apply Studio 2.0 blue theme, `rs-studio-*` classes, or `studio-design-tokens.css` here
- Treat as a separate embedded application

## When editing

- Studio 2.0 visual passes → scope to `.ops-studio-page` only
- Library/browser table work → keep VirtualDJ Browser styling isolated
- Browser+ 2 may use Studio tokens for Mission Control chrome; link out to `/ops/browser-plus` for full VDJ browser
